language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find three cards that form a set: for each of the four features, the three cards show that feature either all the same or all different. Print the indices of the three cards (0-based), in increasing order.
given cards_data_dim1, cards_data_dim2 : int(1..)
given cards_data : matrix indexed by [int(1..cards_data_dim1), int(1..cards_data_dim2)] of int
find winning_cards : matrix indexed by [int(1..3)] of int(0..cards_data_dim1-1)

branching on [winning_cards]

such that
$ the three cards are different cards, listed in increasing order (a set of three cards)
allDiff(winning_cards),
(winning_cards[1] < winning_cards[2]),
(winning_cards[2] < winning_cards[3]),
$ for every feature, the three cards are all the same or all different in that feature
forAll f : int(1..cards_data_dim2) . (((cards_data[winning_cards[1] + 1, f] = cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f]) /\ (cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f] = cards_data[winning_cards[3] + 1, f])) \/ allDiff([cards_data[winning_cards[1] + 1, f], cards_data[winning_cards[2] + 1, f], cards_data[winning_cards[3] + 1, f]]))
